  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed change of use would result in the loss of a C3 residential flat and community facility. Additionally, it has not been demonstrated that an alternative, more appropriate locations are available for the proposed nursery. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies H8 of the London Plan (2021), DMD4, DMD16 and DMD18 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and Enfield Local Housing Need Assessment (2020) which seek to resist the loss of housing.",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of a noise report and acceptable mitigation measures fails to demonstrate how the proposed change of use would manage and operate to reduce exposure to noise and would result in detrimental amenity impacts to future neighbouring residential properties contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D14 of the London Plan (2021), CP32 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD4, DMD16, DMD18 and DMD68 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of an adequate transport assessment and acceptable mitigation measures would result in an unacceptable trip generation, that would increase traffic levels and negatively impact the free flow of traffic and compromise highway safety contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T2, T3, T4, T6 and T6.2 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "In the absence of a legal agreement restricting future occupiers to apply for parking permits, the proposal would not offer a mechanism to mitigate the parking stress in a Controlled Parking Zone. The proposal would therefore contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T2, T3, T4, T6 and T6.2 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
